Condition : 5 - Prior to the completion of the approved conversion from A2 to D1 use, details of hard and soft landscaping works for the formation of a rear amenity space shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The works shall then be carried out as approved.

The detailed landscaping scheme shall include (as applicable):
- soft planting: including any turfed areas, trees, shrubs or herbaceous planting including details of species;
- hard landscaping: including ground surfaces, outdoor furniture, paved steps and waste/ recycling points;
- fences, walls, gates and any other boundary treatments;
- any children's play equipment;
- any signage;
- any CCTV equipment or outdoor lighting;
- details of the proposed erection of a rear lean-to covering (including materials and detailed Proposed Plans/ Proposed Elevations).

Any planting comprised in the approved details shall be carried out during the first planting and seeding seasons following completion of construction works. Any trees or shrubs planted (including any such replacements) which die within three years from the date of planting shall be replaced in the next planting season with the same species, and of comparable maturity. The development shall be carried out strictly in accordance with the details so approved and shall be maintained in accordance with the approved management programme.
